      "id": "community",
      "title": "A rumour at supper",
      "giver": "inn",
      "offer": "Maren hears a rumour that the mill has stopped delivering supplies. If she cancels tonight, the neighbourhood gathering will fall apart. “I need more than the loudest voice in the room. Will you find out what we know?”",
      "done": "Maren keeps the gathering on and explains exactly what the two records support. The supper table is laid. The neighbours agree to bring dated examples when they raise tomorrow’s concerns.",
      "reward": {
        "gold": 40,
        "xp": 12
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "location": "millhouse",
          "target": "resident",
          "title": "Ask Rook at the millhouse",
          "text": "Rook shows you today’s signed dispatch entry: one delivery left the mill at noon. “That tells you it left here. It does not, by itself, prove it arrived.”",
          "after": "You write the account in your quest journal. Follow the next lead at the Copper Oven."
        },
        {
          "location": "bakery",
          "target": "ledger",
          "title": "Examine the household ledger",
          "text": "Pell’s household ledger records the same delivery arriving at the Copper Oven at one. The recipient signed beside the matching delivery number. An unsigned margin note says “nothing ever arrives”, without a date or event.",
          "after": "You now have both pieces of evidence. Return to the Amber Lantern supper table."
        },
        {
          "location": "inn",
          "target": "workbench",
          "title": "Prepare the household plan",
          "text": "You lay the notes beside each other. The neighbours are waiting for a plan they can use.",
          "after": "The matching dispatch and receipt support the claim about today’s delivery. They do not establish a universal claim about every delivery.",
          "challenge": {
            "type": "choice",
            "prompt": "Choose the update Maren can give the guests.",
            "options": [
              "Cancel: an unsigned complaint outweighs the dated records.",
              "Say today’s delivery is recorded at dispatch and receipt; do not claim every delivery is reliable.",
              "Promise that the mill can never miss a delivery."
            ],
            "solution": 1,
            "hint": "Use the dated records for the event they describe. One confirmed case cannot prove “always”.",
            "explanation": "The matching dispatch and receipt support the claim about today’s delivery. They do not establish a universal claim about every delivery."
          }
        },
        {
          "location": "inn",
          "target": "resident",
          "title": "Return to Maren",
          "text": "Your work is ready. Explain the plan and let the household put it into practice.",
          "after": "The neighbours can carry on."
        }
      ]
    },
